## 5. Adaptive Spawning: The Exact Thresholds Are Published

This is the part where your instinct about latency ("api calls only") is correct, and the numbers are specific.

| Decision | Research threshold | Source |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Spawn at all?** | Only when the subtask exceeds **~15 minutes of single-agent time** | AgentSpawn cost-benefit analysis |
| **Spawn cost** | **80ms** fixed overhead per spawn (20 tokens) | M8 sub-agent delegation spike |
| **Full serialization cost** | **2–5 seconds** per spawn (serialization + memory slicing + child init) | AgentSpawn |
| **When spawn kills ROI** | Simple tasks — *"Spawn overhead (80ms, 20 tokens) kills ROI on simple tasks"* | M8 |
| **Accuracy lift when it works** | **+20%** on complex reasoning | M8 |
| **Latency budget required** | ≥500ms to absorb the 35–45% overhead | M8 |
| **Runtime fan-out N** | **3–7** sub-questions, chosen at runtime | L4a parallel fan-out |
| **Spawn depth limit** | **3 levels** (parent → child → grandchild); deeper risks coordination overhead | AgentSpawn |
| **Per-child timeout** | **30 minutes** max | AgentSpawn |
| **Semantic merge success** | **73%** — highly coupled modifications remain challenging | AgentSpawn |

**The spawning decision tree this gives you:**

```
Is the subtask > ~15 min of single-agent work?
  ├── NO  → Do it inline. Spawn overhead (80ms–5s) exceeds the benefit.
  └── YES → Is the task shape KNOWN and DETERMINISTIC?
              ├── YES → Wide fan-out: N = 3–7 parallel workers
              │         (read-only branches only if speculative)
              └── NO  → Recursive: spawn 1 child to go deeper,
                         evaluate the result, decide whether to recurse again
                         (max depth 3)
```

And a cost result that matters for a personal budget: AgentSpawn reports **+54% tokens, +92% API calls, +44% time** per task versus a single agent — but **−9% cost per *successful* completion** because the completion rate goes from **45% → 67%**. Multi-agent is *more expensive per attempt* and *cheaper per success* — which is the correct way to evaluate it.

